From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu <edwardzhu@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:18:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] OSLoader: dual-boot menu (HP OS / NuttX) with NuttX path
 verified

- New BOOTMENU variant: menu firmware linked at 0x30000, started by the
  BootROM through LDLB. NuttX is loaded from NAND block 243 into 0x0.
- Keep the menu's exception vectors at 0x0 until IRQs are off: the image's
  first 64 bytes (vector block) are written only right before the jump,
  otherwise a FreeRTOS tick vectors into the uninitialised NuttX handlers
  and the machine resets back to the menu.
- Park TIMROT/LCDIF/APBH/GPMI/ECC8/ICOLL in reset before jumping so stale
  interrupts (IRQ 28 TIMER0, IRQ 45 LCDIF_DMA) cannot reach NuttX's
  irq_unexpected_isr.
- Keep the HP OS entry as "unavail": the vendor boot stream relies on the
  mask-ROM/high-vector environment and still hangs from the menu. The
  experimental path is compiled only with BOOTMENU_HP.
- NXB1 header for the NuttX segment, image size guard, BOOTMENU_AUTO debug
  build for deterministic QEMU tests.
